record templartorrent.papercut.a-multi-file-patch-for-allocation-telemetry/1 : papercut {
    title "A multi-file patch for allocation telemetry missed a context line after…"
    state verified
    statement """
        A multi-file patch for allocation telemetry missed a context line after rustfmt changed the metric print layout. The patch was atomic; re-read the formatted lines and applied the changes in smaller patches.
        """
    observed_at git:72b01427f8bb0ef32794e5ecc67fe6a3dae2912e
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-10-15
}

record templartorrent.papercut.akr-read-context-accept-revision-qualified/1 : papercut {
    title "AKR read/context accept revision-qualified references, but revise and…"
    state verified
    statement """
        AKR read/context accept revision-qualified references, but revise and complete require the bare key. Passing /3 or /1 was rejected; reran mutations with bare keys. Scratch prune ran after those errors, so recreated the status overlay from the preserved handoff artifact before retrying.
        """
    observed_at git:72b01427f8bb0ef32794e5ecc67fe6a3dae2912e
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-10-15
}

record templartorrent.papercut.akr-strict-validation-flags-observations/1 : papercut {
    title "AKR strict validation flags observations watching new engine/storage…"
    state verified
    statement """
        AKR strict validation flags observations watching new engine/storage directories because observed_at anchors HEAD before these untracked paths exist. Use a tracked parent glob until code is committed; dirty watched paths also emit the expected G004 freshness warning.
        """
    observed_at git:72b01427f8bb0ef32794e5ecc67fe6a3dae2912e
    author "codex"
    created_at 2026-10-15
}

record templartorrent.papercut.capturing-the-templartorrent-window-on-display/1 : papercut {
    title "Capturing the TemplarTorrent window on DISPLAY=:1 failed the first…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Capturing the TemplarTorrent window on DISPLAY=:1 failed the first script because import, scrot, and xwd are not installed (set -e exited before launch). ffmpeg x11grab of the xwininfo geometry worked. xdotool search --name TemplarTorrent also matches the pcmanfm desktop icon, so the window has to be found by pid.
        """
    observed_at git:72b01427f8bb0ef32794e5ecc67fe6a3dae2912e
    about "x11"
    author "grok"
    created_at 2026-10-17
}

record templartorrent.papercut.committing-the-resume-bitmap-failed-with-author/1 : papercut {
    title "Committing the resume bitmap failed with \"Author identity unknown\"…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Committing the resume bitmap failed with "Author identity unknown" because this repository has no local user.name or user.email, and the environment did not set them either. History is entirely dk <dkoepke@protonmail.com>. The commit went through by passing those as GIT_AUTHOR_* and GIT_COMMITTER_* for that command, without writing git config.
        """
    observed_at git:f1d59c5a23138dd76b7509100baf43a2ed10292e
    about "git"
    author "grok"
    created_at 2026-10-22
}

record templartorrent.papercut.in-integration-rbit-adapter-tests-driver-rs-the/1 : papercut {
    title "In integration/rbit-adapter/tests/driver.rs the `hold` fixture fault…"
    state verified
    statement """
        In integration/rbit-adapter/tests/driver.rs the `hold` fixture fault parks on `std::future::pending()` inside its request handler, so it stops reading after the first request and `stats.requests` never grows past one. A test waiting for four requests from a hold server hits its deadline. Added a `silent` fault that records requests and keeps reading for pipeline-depth assertions.
        """
    observed_at git:72b01427f8bb0ef32794e5ecc67fe6a3dae2912e
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-10-22
}

record templartorrent.papercut.knowledge-revise-accepted-an-observation-whose/1 : papercut {
    title "knowledge.revise accepted an observation whose observed_at named a…"
    state verified
    statement """
        knowledge.revise accepted an observation whose observed_at named a commit that does not exist, and wrote the revision; only the next `akr check` reported AKR-G011. knowledge.propose rejects the same input up front. revise should run the same commit-presence check before writing.
        """
    observed_at git:12637360df87a4a1edc2b12c067f803f52df957c
    about "akr"
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-10-26
}

record templartorrent.papercut.knowledge-start-and-knowledge-search-with/1 : papercut {
    title "`knowledge.start` and `knowledge.search` with planning kinds returned…"
    state verified
    statement """
        `knowledge.start` and `knowledge.search` with planning kinds returned nothing because the ledger held only two completed milestones and no live planning record for AGENTS.md step 4; the handoff state lived in a stale observation and in perf-results handoff.json files. Opened templartorrent.milestone.safety-and-peer-policy so the next session has a live key to pass to knowledge.context.
        """
    observed_at git:72b01427f8bb0ef32794e5ecc67fe6a3dae2912e
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-10-22
}

