record templartorrent.papercut.resuming-from-the-ledger-the-inherited/1 : papercut {
    title "Resuming from the ledger, the inherited uncommitted tree failed `cargo…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Resuming from the ledger, the inherited uncommitted tree failed `cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets -D warnings` with three lints in templartorrent-storage and the adapter, although the latest evidence records said Clippy passed; the tree drifted after that evidence was recorded. Running the gates before trusting an evidence record for an uncommitted tree is the only defence until the tree is committed.
        """
    observed_at git:72b01427f8bb0ef32794e5ecc67fe6a3dae2912e
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-10-22
}

record templartorrent.papercut.running-akr-evidence-add-many-with-records-that/1 : papercut {
    title "Running akr evidence add-many with records that lack observed_at…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Running akr evidence add-many with records that lack observed_at printed two AKR-T022 errors and 'nothing written', then '3 evidence records written in one pass' on the next line although nothing was written; the success line should not print after a refused pass, and the help text could say add-many does not default observed_at to HEAD the way evidence add does.
        """
    observed_at git:dfa95bf6a1104f6761a67d115f7ee640838841d3
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-11-03
}

record templartorrent.papercut.running-the-rbit-fork-s-own-cargo-test-lib/1 : papercut {
    title "Running the rbit fork's own `cargo test --lib` without features fails…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Running the rbit fork's own `cargo test --lib` without features fails to compile ("cannot find type HttpTracker") because a test module still refers to it unconditionally after the fork made http-client optional; `--features http-client` builds and passes 160 tests. Running it in-tree also needs a copy outside vendor/rbit, or it writes a crate-local Cargo.lock that the fork notes say was removed.
        """
    observed_at git:a86c4fc56874e2f511dd38623afd5810cad7056c
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-10-24
}

record templartorrent.papercut.running-the-workspace-tests-with-tmpdir-on-a/1 : papercut {
    title "Running the workspace tests with TMPDIR on a real disk (to exercise…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Running the workspace tests with TMPDIR on a real disk (to exercise storage on btrfs instead of tmpfs /tmp) fails ui::tests::paste_magnet_from_the_system_clipboard and window_close_saves_layout_and_resume with "path must be shorter than SUN_LEN": the activation listener's Unix socket lives under temp_dir(), so a TMPDIR under the repository is too long. Those two tests need a short socket directory independent of TMPDIR.
        """
    observed_at git:a86c4fc56874e2f511dd38623afd5810cad7056c
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-10-24
}

record templartorrent.papercut.session-set-wanted-only-re-evaluated-job/1 : papercut {
    title "Session::set_wanted only re-evaluated job completion when a piece…"
    state verified
    statement """
        Session::set_wanted only re-evaluated job completion when a piece verified or a recheck finished, so a restored job whose saved selection was applied after its recheck stayed Downloading with everything it wanted already on disk; the same stall affected a live job that deselects its last incomplete file. Fixed with resettle_completion in the engine and a regression test; anyone adding a new selection mutator must call it too.
        """
    observed_at git:bc5a25057784b680316a863936561d5836a65716
    author "claude"
    created_at 2026-10-22
}

record templartorrent.papercut.the-peer-score-acceptance-command-used-cargo/1 : papercut {
    title "The peer-score acceptance command used cargo test --test with the test…"
    state verified
    statement """
        The peer-score acceptance command used cargo test --test with the test function name. Cargo treats --test as an integration-test target, so it exited 101 with no target named driver_corruption_retries_verified_piece_without_corrupting_files. The target is driver; the function name is a filter before --.
        """
    observed_at git:0c9c0ed8bf04f3d5fdbea28a708ecbe5b8bef368
    about "cargo"
    author "grok"
    created_at 2026-10-22
}

